DiskSweep privileged helper — install SPEC (SMJobBless)

WHY: standard users cannot move /Library/Application Support/* rows to
Trash. The helper exists ONLY for that. Scanner never runs as root.

CHECKLIST (Xcode 16+, paid Apple Developer account):
1. Targets: app (com.nitedsp.disksweep) + helper tool
   (com.nitedsp.disksweep.helper, LaunchDaemons plist).
2. Both sign with same Team ID; helper gets Info.plist SMPrivilegedExecutables
   entry mirrored in app's launchd plist (SMAuthorizedClients).
3. Helper links ../scanner/policy.hpp (already does) — refuses BLOCKED +
   non-Trash dst even if the app is compromised.
4. Install prompt fires ONLY when user checks a /Library/* row and presses
   Move to Trash (consent sheet first, per-item list).
5. Uninstall: app removal unloads helper; QA must verify no leftover daemon.

WITHOUT signing (dev): helper.cpp compiles standalone for logic tests:
  clang++ -std=c++17 -I../scanner helper.cpp -o /tmp/ds-helper
  echo '{"src":"/tmp/x","dst":"$HOME/.Trash/Disksweep/t/x"}' | /tmp/ds-helper
